in ; cuobjdump -sass ; addresses stripped\n\nkernels/indexer.cu   pre   5847 lines   post   5847 lines   IDENTICAL\nkernels/compressed_decode.cu pre  12612 lines   post  12612 lines   IDENTICAL\n\nsha256 of the stripped SASS:\nc9c877f122934ecd6d7e1ca001750eecfe2458aa26dc2071043b4f01ec098440  compressed_decode.post.sass\nc9c877f122934ecd6d7e1ca001750eecfe2458aa26dc2071043b4f01ec098440  compressed_decode.pre.sass\nacbb6c88daec6280fbbc64026d2378e673981d86686f4549fec893ca872bcf34  indexer.post.sass\nacbb6c88daec6280fbbc64026d2378e673981d86686f4549fec893ca872bcf34  indexer.pre.sass\n\nCONCLUSION: item 1.4 changed no device code. Every kernel in both translation units compiles\nto byte-identical SASS; the only change is the host-side launch CONFIGURATION of the four\nfallback/reference launches (dynamic shared memory opt-in + a post-launch error check), and\nthe shipped radix branch does not evaluate either macro. Bit-exactness is therefore a property\nof the compiled artefact here, not an inference from a token comparison.\n=== build log ===\n7:built build/decode\n8:DECODE_RC=0\n9:built build/gate_tokenizer","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
