{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDthboGM18YzSJXiaTDv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ju9dhZ8GgUss7ti2im8LLU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/ladder_1p4.py <<'PYEOF'\np='DECODE_LADDER.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"- [ ] **1.4** `cudaFuncSetAttribute` opt-in for dynamic shared memory, or drop the requirement\n      entirely (1.2 does). Removes a silent garbage-return above ~49k context.\n      **NARROWED, NOT CLOSED, by 1.2 (2026-08-20).** The shipped path now requests **zero** dynamic\n      shared memory — the radix select uses ~7 KiB of *static* shared memory whatever T is — so the\n      ~49k ceiling cannot be hit by the kernel the engine runs. It is deliberately left unchecked\n      because that is a mechanical fact about the launch, **not a measurement**: nothing in this\n      repo has run the engine above 49k context, `seqmax` is 16,384, and the two paths that still\n      ask for `topk_scan_smem(T)` — the `DSV4_TOPK_RADIX=0` fallback arm and the `DSV4_TOPK_GATE=1`\n      reference — retain the defect. Close this item by either deleting those paths or opting them\n      in, and by running one leg above the ceiling.\n\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"- [x] **1.4** `cudaFuncSetAttribute` opt-in for dynamic shared memory — **DONE 2026-08-20,\n      iteration 5. OPTED IN, NOT DELETED. Ceiling 49,140 -> 232,436 tokens of context (4.7x), and\n      above that it aborts instead of returning garbage. NO THROUGHPUT CLAIM, and none is possible:\n      the two changed translation units compile to BYTE-IDENTICAL SASS.**\n\n      **THIS IS THE SECOND CONSECUTIVE ITERATION WITHOUT A KERNEL CHANGE (rule 5).** 1.3 shipped a\n      kernel change worth nothing; 1.4 ships no kernel change at all. Rule 5 says to say so at the\n      top of the entry and take the highest-expected-value kernel item next even if it is less\n      certain — that is **1.5** (`i:score` as a GEMM + fused epilogue), and the re-attribution below\n      confirms it is still the right one. 1.4 was done anyway because it is the topmost unchecked\n      item and it is a correctness item with a bounded cost, not because it was expected to pay.\n\n      **THE DEFECT, MEASURED RATHER THAN INFERRED.** The ladder said \"silent garbage-return above\n      ~49k context\". It is worse than \"silent\" in the specific way that matters:\n\n      | T | dynamic smem | `cudaGetLastError()` after launch | `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` | output buffer |\n      |---:|---:|---|---|---|\n      | 12,288 | 49,152 B | `cudaSuccess` | `cudaSuccess` | correct |\n      | 16,384 | 65,536 B | **`cudaErrorInvalidValue`** | **`cudaSuccess`** | **untouched** |\n\n      A shared-memory over-request is rejected at *launch configuration* time, on the host, before\n      anything is enqueued — so there is no device work to fault and **the synchronize reports\n      success**. `dprobe()` is inert without `DSV4_SYNCPROBE`; `dsync()` only warns without\n      `DSV4_STRICT_LAUNCH` and skips its sync entirely while the arena is on. The consumer would\n      have read `zalloc`'s zeros and `sparse_attn` would have attended to KV row 0 for every head,\n      at full speed, forever. See `wiki/measurement-and-traps.md` §17.\n\n      **THE DECISION: OPT IN, NOT DELETE.** Deleting the four warp kernels also closes the item and\n      is fewer lines. It also deletes the `DSV4_TOPK_RADIX=0` A/B arm and the `DSV4_TOPK_GATE=1`\n      in-situ reference — the only thing in this repo that can prove a *future* top-k change still\n      matches the original selection sort, and the instrument 1.2 and 1.3 were both gated on. An\n      instrument that returns zeros above a context nobody has tried is worse than no instrument,\n      because it agrees with anything. The reference is worth more than the twelve lines.\n\n      **WHAT SHIPPED.** `topk_scan_smem_optin()` / `TOPK_SMEM()` / `TOPK_LAUNCHED()` in\n      `include/indexer.h`, applied at all **six** launch sites that request `topk_scan_smem(T)`\n      (`indexer.cu` k_topk_offset; `compressed_decode.cu` k_topk_decode x2, k_topk_verify x2,\n      k_topk_masked). It (a) returns immediately when the request fits the default limit — so the\n      entire reachable regime adds **zero** CUDA calls; (b) opts the kernel in **once, ever**, to\n      the device maximum, so the A/B arm gains no per-launch host overhead that would inflate future\n      re-measurements of 1.2; (c) **aborts with the numbers** above the opt-in maximum rather than\n      sizing a launch that cannot run; (d) drains and reports the error slot before the launch and\n      checks it after, so a configuration failure is attributed to the launch that caused it.\n\n      | limit on this device | bytes | T | context at ratio 4 |\n      |---|---:|---:|---:|\n      | `cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlock` (default) | 49,152 | 12,285 | **49,140** |\n      | `cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin` | 232,448 | 58,109 | **232,436** |\n\n      **THE LEG ABOVE THE CEILING, which the item asked for, is now a standing gate.**\n      `tests/gate_topk_radix.cu` (already in `build_gate.sh`, `decode_loop.sh` and\n      `decode_loop_watchdog.sh`, so it runs every iteration from now on) gained four legs — the\n      first is the one that matters, because it asserts the *defect* and will fail if a future CUDA\n      release changes the failure mode out from under this entry:\n\n      | leg | result |\n      |---|---|\n      | no opt-in, T=16,381 | launch `cudaErrorInvalidValue`, sync `cudaSuccess`, output UNTOUCHED — **defect reproduced** |\n      | opted in, T=12,286 / 16,381 / 24,570 / **58,045** (49 KiB .. **232 KiB**, context up to **232,180**) | identical to the radix select on all 6 distributions, early-out ON and OFF |\n      | under CUDA-graph capture, T=16,381 | captured, replayed, identical — `k_topk_masked` is on the captured `_dp` path, so this was a real risk |\n      | above the opt-in maximum, T=59,133 | forked child dies on **SIGABRT** — the refusal is exercised, not decorated |\n\n      Exactly **one** `[topk-smem]` opt-in line appears in the whole gate run, which is the\n      once-per-kernel property demonstrated rather than asserted.\n\n      **BIT-EXACTNESS: PROVED ON THE COMPILED ARTEFACT, NOT ON TOKENS.** Invariant 1 was amended by\n      1.0 because token ids are not a valid test at context. Here there is something stronger and\n      cheaper than either: `nvcc -cubin` + `cuobjdump -sass` on both changed translation units,\n      HEAD vs working tree, addresses stripped —\n\n      | TU | SASS lines | sha256 |\n      |---|---:|---|\n      | `kernels/indexer.cu` | 5,847 = 5,847 | `acbb6c88…` = `acbb6c88…` |\n      | `kernels/compressed_decode.cu` | 12,612 = 12,612 | `c9c877f1…` = `c9c877f1…` |\n\n      **No device code changed.** The change is host-side launch configuration on branches the\n      shipped path does not take: with `DSV4_TOPK_RADIX` at its default the `if` arm runs and\n      neither macro is evaluated. `evidence/decode_loop/sass_1p4_identical.txt`.\n\n      **tau: NOT MEASURED, AND DELIBERATELY NOT.** Invariant 2 requires tau in every A/B. There is\n      no A/B here — there is no arm to compare, because the shipped device code is the same bytes\n      and the shipped host path issues the same calls. A checkpoint load to re-measure a quantity\n      that provably cannot have moved would be ~10 minutes of GPU for a number already on record.\n      **If any future reader disagrees with that reasoning, the thing to distrust is the SASS\n      comparison, and it is reproducible in two minutes with the command in the evidence file.**\n\n      **WHAT WAS FOUND AND NOT FIXED, stated so it is not rediscovered as new.**\n      * `sdpa()` in `kernels/attention.cu` has the identical defect — `shmem = (head_dim + seq) *\n        sizeof(float)`, a context-sized dynamic request with no opt-in. It is **dead code**: the\n        symbol has no caller anywhere in `src/` or `kernels/`. Not fixed, not deleted, recorded here.\n      * Every other dynamic-shared launch in the engine is sized by a fixed model constant\n        (`n_routed`, `threads`, `HEAD_DIM`), not by context. `k_topk_masked` on the `_dp` graph path\n        is sized by `Tmax = seqmax/ratio` rather than the live `T`, so *its* ceiling is a ceiling on\n        **`seqmax`**, not on the current context — noted at the call site.\n\n      **RE-ATTRIBUTION FOR THE NEXT ITERATION (rule 6).** Nothing in 1.4 touches arithmetic, so the\n      1.3 cost model stands unchanged and is repeated here so the next iteration does not have to\n      go looking: `draft:main_kv` **-0.000** (spent), `i:topk` **0.084 +/- 0.001** (spent),\n      `cattn:sparse` **1.694 +/- 0.065** over ctx 0.4k-6k but *concave — read rule 7, the lever\n      there is the ~20 ms floor, not the slope*, `i:score` **0.629 +/- 0.018 and genuinely linear**\n      (0.482 then 0.495 ms per 1000 across two legs). **1.5 is next and its rank is unchanged.**\n\n      Evidence: `evidence/decode_loop/gate_topk_smem_1p4.log` (the four new legs),\n      `sass_1p4_identical.txt` (device-code equivalence), `gates_1p4.log` (standing gates, both\n      `DSV4_TOPK_RADIX` arms), `build_1p4.log`.\n      Wiki: `measurement-and-traps.md` §17, `context-ceiling-is-not-the-kv-cache.md` (\"The second\n      ceiling, which is not memory at all\"), `README.md` state table.\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s, \"ladder anchor not found\"\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ladder updated\")\nPYEOF\necho staged","description":"Stage ladder entry patch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":134593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c5f1c60-b2a5-44bb-bd1f-9a1d9ec21225","uuid":"a1528136-286b-4560-8aab-32c687d3bfe6","timestamp":"2026-08-20T11:06:51.116Z","request_id":"req_011CeDthaAYBKqzKM5yL5fYU"}
