{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDtqqprGDrPEkGxggD6X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The builds are still running (the server TU takes several minutes on this box). While they finish, here's where iteration 5 stands:\n\n**Item 1.4 — done, opted in rather than deleted.**\n\nThe defect is now measured rather than asserted:\n\n| T | dynamic smem | `cudaGetLastError()` after launch | `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` | output buffer |\n|---:|---:|---|---|---|\n| 12,288 | 49,152 B | `cudaSuccess` | `cudaSuccess` | correct |\n| 16,384 | 65,536 B | **`cudaErrorInvalidValue`** | **`cudaSuccess`** | **untouched** |\n\nA shared-memory over-request is rejected at launch-configuration time on the host, so nothing is enqueued and the synchronize reports success. That defeats every existing defence: `dprobe()` is inert without `DSV4_SYNCPROBE`, `dsync()` only warns without `DSV4_STRICT_LAUNCH`, and it skips its sync entirely while the arena is on.\n\n**What shipped:** `topk_scan_smem_optin()` / `TOPK_SMEM()` / `TOPK_LAUNCHED()` in `include/indexer.h`, at all six `topk_scan_smem(T)` launch sites. Ceiling 49,140 → 232,436 tokens of context; above that it aborts with the numbers instead of sizing an impossible launch. Zero added CUDA calls in the reachable regime (early return under the default limit), one opt-in per kernel for the process lifetime so the `DSV4_TOPK_RADIX=0` A/B arm gains no per-launch overhead.\n\n**The leg above the ceiling is now a standing gate** in `tests/gate_topk_radix.cu` — four new legs, all passing: defect reproduced without opt-in; bit-identical to the radix select at T = 12,286 / 16,381 / 24,570 / 58,045 (up to 232 KiB of smem, context 232,180) on six distributions with the 1.3 early-out both on and off; identical under CUDA-graph capture (`k_topk_masked` is on the captured `_dp` path); and a forked child dying on `SIGABRT` above the opt-in maximum, so the refusal is exercised rather than decorative.\n\n**Bit-exactness proved on the compiled artefact:** `cuobjdump -sass` of both changed TUs, HEAD vs working tree, is byte-identical (`indexer.cu` 5,847 lines `acbb6c88…`; `compressed_decode.cu` 12,612 lines `c9c877f1…`). No device code changed, so no throughput or tau claim is possible or made — I'll say that explicitly rather than burn a checkpoint load re-measuring a number that provably cannot have moved.\n\nTwo things I found and did **not** fix, recorded so they aren't rediscovered as new: `sdpa()` in `kernels/attention.cu` has the identical defect but is dead code with no caller anywhere; and `k_topk_masked` on the `_dp` path is sized by `Tmax = seqmax/ratio`, so its ceiling is on `seqmax`, not live context.\n\nFlagging per ladder rule 5: **this is the second consecutive iteration with no kernel change.** 1.3 shipped one worth nothing, 1.4 ships none at all. The re-attribution is unchanged (`i:score` 0.629 ± 0.018 and genuinely linear), so 1.5 — `i:score` as a GEMM with a fused epilogue — is next and keeps its rank.\n\nWiki, ladder entry and commit are staged; they land once the build finishes and the standing gates run on both `DSV4_TOPK_RADIX` arms."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":371,"cache_read_input_tokens":144651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":371},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c5f1c60-b2a5-44bb-bd1f-9a1d9ec21225","uuid":"206abd22-4cf5-42df-9305-abac28b435ca","timestamp":"2026-08-20T11:08:12.326Z","request_id":"req_011CeDtqpsJVevgQyzqcThoB"}
